-- title:
--   Rigidity of the Ω-datum along a square-zero thickening
-- statement:
--   The statement is a uniqueness assertion for the Deligne datum attached to a rigidified fake elliptic curve over a square-zero thickening, formulated inside the full Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison package. The hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Primes and level** ($hrr$, $hrN$, $hrbarN$, $hN$). Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   **Coefficients** ($hdvr$, $h\pi$, $hcomplete$, $hres$, $hunr$; $K_0$; $hOnr\_*$, $hFr$; $hvdet$). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, $\#(\mathcal O/\pi) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$; a characteristic-zero field of fractions $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. Further, a characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$; thus $Onr$ plays the role of the ring of integers of the completed maximal unramified extension together with its Frobenius. Finally a homomorphism $vdet : GL_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by: $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The indefinite quaternion side and its moduli** ($hB$, $h\Lambda$, $h\Lambda\mathbb Z$; $h\mathcal X$; $hn$, $hrn$, $hrbarn$, $hnN$, $hM$, $h\rho$; $hp$, $h\rho p$, $hp\_pt$; $h\mathcal Y$, $hd_0f$, $hd_1f$, $hd_0$, $hd_1$; $harf$, $harbarf$, $har$, $harbar$). Rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and is a division algebra locally exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ containing all rational integers. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point assignment $pt$ exhibiting it as a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves for $(\Lambda, N)$ (isomorphism invariance, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$, a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $ptF$ a fine moduli structure for fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure, and a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ forming a level-twist action. A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over the base, invariant under $\rho$, and compatible with the two point assignments. For every prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with extra $\ell$-level structure, together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base, $d_0$ inducing the forgetting of the $\ell$-level and $d_1$ the passage along an $\ell$-level isogeny. Endomorphisms $ar$, $arbar$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base inducing on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$.
--
--   **The definite quaternion side** ($hdef$, $h\Lambda_1$, $hR_1$, $hR\Lambda_1$, $hn_1$, $hS_1$, $h\iota_0$, $hv$; $h\Gamma t$, $hs$, $h\Gamma t\ell$; $hwbar$). Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$, an adelic unit $n_1$ in the $r$-th Hecke set of $R_1$ such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ and a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma t$ of the unit group equal to the group of units integral away from $v$ for $R_1$; for each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ elements $s(\ell)$ and adelic units $sf(\ell)$ whose four clauses require that $sf(\ell)$ is $s(\ell)$ locally away from $r$, is trivial at $r$, that the diagonal image of $\ell$ times $sf(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ relative to $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the $\ell$-th Hecke set of that order otherwise, and that the reduced norm of $s(\ell)$ is $\ell$; the groups $\Gamma t_\ell = \Gamma t \cap s(\ell)\Gamma t s(\ell)^{-1}$; an element $wbar$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma t$.
--
--   **The special fibre at $r$** ($coord$, $hcoord$; $hX_0$, $hA_0$; $he$, $deg$; $hE1$, $hE1mul$, $hE1sc$, $hE1'$, $hE2$, $hE3$, $hE4$; the $R_2$-package $hR_2$, $hR_2o$, $hR_2r$, $h\hat e$, $hE5a$–$hE5e$). A coordinate map $coord : \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{r,2} \times \mathbb{Z}_{r,2}$ which is additive, injective, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative in the twisted sense, has dense image modulo all powers of $r$ and computes reduced traces. A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over $Onr/\pi$, two-dimensional formal coordinates $\theta_0$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and the hypothesis that $A_0$ is a formal module via $coord$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Endomorphisms $e(\gamma), e'(\gamma)$ of $A_0$ over the base for $\gamma \in \Gamma t$ with degrees $deg(\gamma)$, subject to: $hE1$ ($e(\gamma), e'(\gamma)$ an $r^{deg\gamma}$-isogeny pair preserving the level structure), $hE1mul$ (multiplicativity up to $r$-power isogenies), $hE1sc$ (scalars in $\Gamma t$ act as the corresponding integers up to $r$-powers), $hE1'$ (only scalars act by a multiplication map), $hE2$ (for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in GL_2(K_0)$ such that each $e(\gamma)$ is realised on formal coordinates by a centraliser element whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), $hE3$ (the $\Gamma t$-action on a full level-$n$ structure is given by $\Lambda$-labels, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$), $hE4$ (over an algebraically closed field every $r$-power isogeny pair preserving the level on a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $\gamma$ up to $r$-powers); and an order $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators relative to $R_1$, acting on $A_0$ by endomorphisms $\hat e$ over the base satisfying additivity and $\Lambda$-equivariance and level preservation ($hE5a$), the unit, product and integer rules ($hE5b1$–$hE5b3$), the norm rule ($hE5c$), compatibility with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma t$ ($hE5d$) and the joint matrix realisation on formal coordinates for both $\Gamma t$ and $R_2$ ($hE5e$).
--
--   **The special formal moduli package** ($h\Phi$, $h\Phi 4$, $hMD$, $h\eta$, $hE_0$). A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{r,2} \to Onr$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ and has height $4$; a moduli package $MD$ over $(r, Onr)$ which is a Zariski sheaf; a family $\eta$ sending rigidified objects to $MD$-points, subject to the three clauses of $h\eta$ (on admissible rigidified objects $\eta$ identifies points exactly when they are isomorphic, $\eta$ is compatible with base change, and every $MD$-point is, locally on a Zariski cover, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$); and a ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ which is injective and, for a single exponent $m$, has image comparable with $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ in both directions ($hE_0$). (The letter $E_0$ is later reused for a fake elliptic curve over $B_0$.)
--
--   **Identification of the moduli functor with the formal upper half-plane** ($eD$, $hnatD$, $hbijD$, $hfstD$, $hGLD$, $hPiD$, $hPiexD$). For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map $eD$ from the $G$-points of $MD$ to pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr \to B$ and a Deligne datum, which is natural in $B$, bijective, has first component the leg $\psi$ of the point, transports the $GL_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points into the twisted action $OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct$ (namely $\psi' = \psi \circ Fr^{-v(\det g)}$ together with the $g^{-1}$-pullback of Deligne data), carries $\pi$-translates to the Frobenius twist of the first component leaving the datum unchanged, and for which $\pi$-translates always exist.
--
--   **Transport data and the Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$** ($\kappa$, $h\kappa$, $n_0$, $\beta_0$, $h\beta_0$; $P_0$; $hALw$, $hBSw$, $hBSwlev$, $hJOINTw$). A ring homomorphism $\kappa$ from $Onr/\pi$ to $Onr/(r)$ compatible with the two quotient maps, and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$; a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; a fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $Onr/\pi$ with morphisms $aw, aw'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$, morphisms $bw, bw'$ forming an $r^{kw}$-isogeny pair back to $A_0$ which preserves the level, and $hJOINTw$, the simultaneous matrix realisation on formal coordinates of the $e(\gamma)$ together with the composite $aw \ggg bw$, the latter matching $r^{k_w}\,g\,\iota_0(wbar)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$ and its properties** ($h\Xi leg$, $h\Xi nat$, $h\Xi iso$, $h\Xi def$; $g_0$, $heq\Gamma$, $heqW$; $hK1$–$hK4$; $hC0e$, $hC0u$). A family $\Xi$ assigning to each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, each $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : Onr \to B$ and each rigidified fake elliptic curve over $(B,\psi)$ a $G$-point of $MD$, such that on $B$ with no nontrivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$, $\Xi$ is natural for pullbacks of rigidified curves, $\Xi$ is unchanged under isomorphisms of rigidified curves admitting the displayed comparison data with $r$-power exponents, and $\Xi$ is computed by $\eta$ applied to a rigidified object obtained by transport along $(\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0)$ with $j \leq 1$. An element $g_0 \in GL_2(K_0)$ for which $\Xi$ turns translation of a rigidification by $e(\gamma)$ into the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ ($heq\Gamma$), and turns an Atkin–Lehner comparison at $\bar r$ with the $aw \ggg bw$-twisted data into the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(wbar)g_0^{-1}$ ($heqW$). The clauses $hK1$–$hK4$ assert, for the twisted leg $\psi \circ Fr^{-v(\det g_0)}$, respectively: existence of a curve with rigidification whose $\Xi$-leg is that twisted leg and whose $eD$-image is carried by $g_0^{-1}$ to a prescribed pair $(\psi,P)$; uniqueness of such a pair up to an isomorphism of rigidified curves of the displayed shape; compatibility with base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; and liftability along a surjection whose kernel has vanishing pairwise products. The clauses $hC0e$, $hC0u$ give existence and uniqueness of the normalised level-$n$ transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification.
--
--   **The point family on $M$** ($\Theta f$, $h\Theta nat$, $h\Theta val$, $h\Theta valc$). A natural family $\Theta f$ of nilpotent points of $fM$ indexed by triples consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $Onr \to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$ and an element $g \in G$, whose value on data satisfying the two evenness conditions and the normalised level transport is the $ptF$-point of the corresponding curve with level structure followed by $\rho(g^{-1})$, and whose composite with $p$ is the $pt$-point of the underlying curve.
--
--   **The data of the assertion.** Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ and $B_0$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in each, a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $pB : B \to B_0$ such that the product of any two elements of its kernel vanishes; an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : Onr \to B$; two Deligne data $P, P'$ over $B$; a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ and two rigidifications $\varrho_1, \varrho_2$ of $E$ relative to the twisted leg $\psi \circ Fr^{-v(\det g_0)}$ — each consisting of a reduction $E_b$ of $E$ over $B/\pi$, a pullback $A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue leg, an exponent $d$ and an $r^{d}$-isogeny pair between $E_b$ and $A_b$ preserving the level. Hypotheses $h_1\psi$ and $h_2\psi$ state that the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho_i)$ is that twisted leg, and $h_1P$, $h_2P$ state that the $eD$-image of $\Xi(E,\varrho_1)$ is carried by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$ to $(\psi,P)$, and that of $\Xi(E,\varrho_2)$ to $(\psi,P')$. Finally a fake elliptic curve $E_0$ over $B_0$ with a morphism $g$ exhibiting $E_0$ as the pullback of $E$ along $pB$, rigidifications $\varrho_{1,0}, \varrho_{2,0}$ of $E_0$ relative to the twisted leg of $pB \circ \psi$ which are pullbacks of $\varrho_1, \varrho_2$ along $(pB, g)$ ($h_1$, $h_2$), and the hypothesis $h_0$: there exist a morphism $ib : \varrho_{1,0}.E_b.A \to \varrho_{2,0}.E_b.A$ with $ib$ followed by $\varrho_{2,0}.g_b$ equal to $\varrho_{1,0}.g_b$ and $ib$ followed by the structure morphism of $\varrho_{2,0}.E_b$ equal to that of $\varrho_{1,0}.E_b$, a morphism $uA : \varrho_{2,0}.A_b.A \to \varrho_{1,0}.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\varrho_{2,0}.A_b$ as a pullback of $\varrho_{1,0}.A_b$ along the identity with $uA$ followed by $\varrho_{1,0}.g_A$ equal to $\varrho_{2,0}.g_A$, and natural numbers $i, j$ with
--   $$ib \ggg \varrho_{2,0}.\varphi \ggg uA \ggg \varrho_{1,0}.A_b.\mathrm{act}(r^{i}) \;=\; \varrho_{1,0}.\varphi \ggg \varrho_{1,0}.A_b.\mathrm{act}(r^{j}),$$
--   all composites taken in diagrammatic order.
--
--   The conclusion is the single equality $P = P'$ of Deligne data over $B$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the local rigidity step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison for the quaternionic (fake elliptic curve) moduli problem: two rigidifications of one curve whose reductions are related by the displayed correspondence over a square-zero thickening determine the same point of the formal upper half-plane functor $\Omega$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero), where the family of points on the fine moduli scheme is shown to be locally uniquely determined by its values.
